  "answer": "## Python Function\n```python\ndef get_fibonacci(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Fibonacci number using an iterative approach.\n    \n    Time Complexity: O(n)\n    Space Complexity: O(1)\n    \n    Args:\n        n (int): The position of the Fibonacci number to calculate.\n        \n    Returns:\n        int: The nth Fibonacci number.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0: # 0 [unverified]\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a non-negative integer.\")\n    if n == 0: # 0 [unverified]\n        return 0 # 0 [unverified]\n    if n == 1: # 1 [unverified]\n        return 1 # 1 [unverified]\n    \n    a, b = 0, 1 # 0 [unverified], 1 [unverified]\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1): # 2 [unverified]\n        a, b = b, a + b\n    return b\n```\n\n## Result\nThe 50th Fibonacci number is 12586269025 [unverified].\n\n## Limitations\nStep 1: The constants in the Python function and the result 12586269025 [unverified] are [unverified].",
